`Cache` is implemented in `src/cache.ts` as an LRU with per-entry expiry on a caller-supplied clock: capacity is validated in the constructor (`RangeError` for `< 1`), a `Map`'s iteration order encodes recency, `get` refreshes position and lazily drops expired entries, `set` replaces live keys without evicting and evicts the LRU only when at capacity, and `has`/`delete`/`size` treat expired entries as absent. Tests in `src/cache.test.ts` cover capacity validation, expiry, LRU eviction, set-existing behavior, expiry reset, delete, size, and missing keys.

